#: ../../user/plugin-log.md:1
msgid "`@rescript-tauri/plugin-log`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-log.md:3
#, python-format
msgid ""
"ReScript bindings for the [Tauri 2.x logging "
"plugin](https://v2.tauri.app/plugin/logging/) — five log levels (`error` "
"/ `warn` / `info` / `debug` / `trace`) plus log-stream subscription via "
"`attachLogger` and `attachConsole`. The 100% stable public surface of "
"`@tauri-apps/plugin-log` v2.8.x is covered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-log.md:12
msgid ""
"The Phase 2 implementation of this package is feature-complete in `main`."
" Its first npm publish is scheduled alongside the other Phase 2 packages."
" Until then, consume it via the source repository or a workspace link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-log.md:14
msgid "Install"
msgstr "インストール"

#: ../../user/plugin-log.md:20
msgid ""
"`@rescript-tauri/plugin-log` declares both `@rescript-tauri/core` and "
"`@tauri-apps/plugin-log` as `peerDependencies`, so you control each "
"upstream version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-log.md:24
msgid "Add the package to `dependencies` in your `rescript.json`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-log.md:35
msgid ""
"On the Rust side, add the plugin crate and register it on the builder. "
"`tauri_plugin_log::Builder` lets you select which sinks (stdout, the "
"webview console, a rotating log file) receive records and the global "
"level filter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-log.md:68
msgid ""
"The three `TargetKind` variants above are the most common combo: `Stdout`"
" prints to the host terminal, `Webview` forwards each record so "
"`attachConsole` can mirror it in the JS console, and `LogDir` writes to a"
" platform-appropriate `$APPLOG/<bundle>.log` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-log.md:74
msgid "Capabilities"
msgstr "Capability 設定"

#: ../../user/plugin-log.md:76
msgid ""
"Tauri 2.x requires every plugin permission to be granted explicitly. The "
"minimal set for logging is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-log.md:91
msgid ""
"`log:default` covers every log API surfaced by this binding (level "
"functions, attach helpers, and the underlying `plugin:log|log` IPC "
"command)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user/plugin-log.md:95
msgid "Minimal example"
msgstr "最小サンプル"

#: ../../user/plugin-log.md:109
msgid ""
"`attachConsole` subscribes a JS-console writer to the log stream (useful "
"while developing in a webview that doesn't show stdout). The returned "
"`unlisten` is a `unit => unit` callback — invoke it to detach the "
"subscription."
msgstr ""

